# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# One file, at the repository root, because all three images build from the root:
# the Rust image needs `Cargo.toml` + `crates/`, the web image needs `web/`, and a
# per-image context would mean three contexts and three copies of this list.
#
# Two reasons an entry is here. Either it is LARGE and would be uploaded to the
# daemon on every build (`target/` is gigabytes, `web/node_modules/` hundreds of
# megabytes), or it is DERIVED and would silently win over the copy the build is
# supposed to produce — `web/build/` from a developer's laptop landing in the image
# instead of the one `npm run build` just made is the kind of difference that only
# shows up in production.

# --- Build artefacts, derived ------------------------------------------------
target/
**/target/
web/build/
web/.svelte-kit/
web/node_modules/
**/node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Runtime state, derived --------------------------------------------------
data/
web/data/
media/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- Never in an image, and several of them never in the repository either ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
secrets-generated/

# --- Repository and agent machinery ------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.forgejo/
.serena/
.claude/
.mcp.json
.mutate-backups/
graphify-out/
GRAPH_*.html

# --- Prose. None of it is read at runtime. -----------------------------------
docs/
webpage/
content-example/
content-darm/
*.md
!crates/**/*.md
